Well, it seems to me that there's an inherent Catch-22 problem.
Soldier ants start appearing around the Oracle or Minetown. Unless
you're lucky (say, an armor emporium on dlvl 2), you probably haven't
had the chance to get really good armor yet. And if you're avoiding
levelling up to avoid tougher monsters, you're also reducing the
chances that a monster will be generated with really good armor to
harvest.

My current Samurai (who has remained Elberethless, other than what I
habitually write when engrave-IDing wands) had -2 AC and was still
taking serious damage from soldier ants. And lots of classes don't
start with as good an AC as a Samurai does.
